#: content/sustainable-goal/_index.md:0
msgid "Sustainable Software Goal"
msgstr "Trajnostni cilj programske opreme"

#: content/sustainable-goal/_index.md:9
msgid ""
"Software has an impact on our future. It has an affect on energy and "
"resource usage. KDE can deliver software which does this in a way which "
"preserves environment and society for us and future generations. KDE can "
"deliver Sustainable Software."
msgstr ""
"Programska oprema ima vpliv na našo bodočnost. Vpliva na rabo energije in "
"virov. KDE lahko dobavlja programsko opremo, ki ohranja okolje, družbo za "
"nas in bodoče generacije. KDE lahko dobavlja trajnostno programsko opremo."

#: content/sustainable-goal/_index.md:11
msgid ""
"The sustainable software goal is about promoting sustainability in KDE by "
"aligning existing activities, highlighting where our software is already "
"sustainably designed, stimulating actions to increase sustainability, and "
"creating standards/tools to quantify software sustainability."
msgstr ""
"Cilj trajnostne programske opreme je spodbujanje trajnosti v KDE z "
"usklajevanjem obstoječih dejavnosti, poudarjanjem, kjer je naša programska "
"oprema že trajnostno zasnovana, spodbujanjem ukrepov za povečanje trajnosti "
"in ustvarjanjem standardov/orodij za količinsko opredelitev trajnosti "
"programske opreme."

#: i18n/en.yaml:0
msgid "Opt Green"
msgstr "Opt Green"

#: i18n/en.yaml:0
msgid ""
"Independent, energy-efficient Free & Open Source Software for long-term "
"hardware use."
msgstr ""
"Neodvisna, energetsko učinkovita prosta in odprtokodna programska oprema za "
"dolgoročno uporabo strojne opreme."

#: i18n/en.yaml:0
msgid "Be Green (End User)"
msgstr "Bodi zelen (končni uporabnik)"

#: i18n/en.yaml:0
msgid ""
"Opt in to lower energy demands, extended hardware life, device independence, "
"and user control for a healthier digital society."
msgstr ""
"Odločite se za manjše energetske zahteve, podaljšano življenjsko dobo "
"strojne opreme, neodvisnost od naprav in uporabniški nadzor za bolj zdravo "
"digitalno družbo."

#: i18n/en.yaml:0
msgid "Grow Green (Advocate)"
msgstr "Rasti zeleno (Zagovornik)"

#: i18n/en.yaml:0
msgid ""
"Build communities and user support networks to bring the benefits of "
"independent, sustainable software to your hometown."
msgstr ""
"Zgradite skupnosti in omrežja za podporo uporabnikom, da bi prednosti "
"neodvisne, trajnostne programske opreme prinesli v svoje domače mesto."

#: i18n/en.yaml:0
msgid "Make Green (Dev)"
msgstr "Razvij zeleno (Razvijalec)"

#: i18n/en.yaml:0
msgid ""
"Develop applications and software features with a focus on efficiency and "
"sustainability for this and future generations."
msgstr ""
"Razvijte aplikacije in zmožnosti programske opreme s poudarkom na "
"učinkovitosti in trajnosti za to in prihodnje generacije."

#: i18n/en.yaml:0
msgid "What makes FOSS sustainable?"
msgstr "Kaj naredi FOSS trajnostnega?"

#: i18n/en.yaml:0
msgid ""
"Free & Open Source Software (FOSS) guarantees transparency and user "
"autonomy, by design. These are not features, but inherent qualities to open "
"development and software licensing. As a result, software and hardware are "
"no longer dependent on vendors for support."
msgstr ""
"Prosta in odprtokodna programska oprema (Free and open source software - "
"FOSS) že po zasnovi zagotavlja preglednost in avtonomijo uporabnika. To niso "
"lastnosti, ampak inherentne lastnosti odprtega razvoja in licenciranja "
"programske opreme. Posledično programska in strojna oprema pri podpori nista "
"več odvisni od prodajalcev."

#: i18n/en.yaml:0
msgid ""
"FOSS can be studied and improved independently, including in its energy "
"consumption. Premature hardware obsolescence is a thing of the past. FOSS "
"runs on devices that are decades old. Keep your computer in use to the end "
"of the hardware operating life, not the software."
msgstr ""
"FOSS je mogoče preučevati in izboljševati neodvisno, vključno z njegovo "
"porabo energije. Prezgodnja zastarelost strojne opreme je preteklost. FOSS "
"deluje na napravah, ki so stare desetletja. Vaš računalnik naj bo v uporabi "
"do konca življenjske dobe strojne opreme in ne programske opreme."

#: i18n/en.yaml:0
msgid "About KDE and KDE Eco"
msgstr "O KDE in KDE Eco"

#: i18n/en.yaml:0
msgid ""
"KDE is a world-wide community of software engineers, artists, writers, "
"translators, and creators who are committed to Free Software development. We "
"are a cooperative enterprise: we work together to achieve the common goal of "
"building the world's finest Free & Open Source Software. Everyone is welcome "
"to join and contribute to KDE, including you."
msgstr ""
"KDE je svetovna skupnost programskih inženirjev, umetnikov, pisateljev, "
"prevajalcev in ustvarjalcev, ki so predani razvoju proste programske opreme. "
"Smo kooperativno podjetje: delamo skupaj, da bi dosegli skupni cilj "
"izgradnje najboljše proste in odprtokodne programske opreme na svetu. Vsi so "
"dobrodošli, vključno z vami, da se pridružite in prispevate k KDE."

#: i18n/en.yaml:0
msgid ""
"Supported by the KDE community since 2021, KDE Eco has the ongoing mission "
"of the development and adoption of sustainable Free & Open Source Software "
"worldwide. As the ecological impact of digitization grows more relevant, we "
"continue to raise awareness about the role of software design in reducing "
"environmental harm. We are proudly a part of a growing number of communities "
"and organizations working to have a positive ecological impact, today."
msgstr ""
"KDE Eco, ki ga od leta 2021 podpira skupnost KDE, ima stalno misijo razvoja "
"in sprejemanja trajnostne proste in odprtokodne programske opreme po vsem "
"svetu. Ker ekološki vpliv digitalizacije postaja vse pomembnejši, še naprej "
"ozaveščamo o vlogi oblikovanja programske opreme pri zmanjševanju okoljske "
"škode. Ponosno smo del vse večjega števila skupnosti in organizacij, ki si "
"danes prizadevajo za pozitiven vpliv na okolje."

#: i18n/en.yaml:0
msgid ""
"Software has a direct affect on energy and resource consumption. Since 2022, "
"KDE has the goal of providing software which does this in a way that reduces "
"software’s environmental impact for us and future generations."
msgstr ""
"Programska oprema neposredno vpliva na porabo energije in virov. Od leta "
"2022 ima KDE cilj zagotoviti programsko opremo, ki to počne na način, ki "
"zmanjšuje vpliv programske opreme na okolje za nas in prihodnje generacije."

#: i18n/en.yaml:0
msgid "Free and open source software Energy Efficiency Project"
msgstr "Projekt energetske učinkovitosti proste in odprte programske opreme"

#: i18n/en.yaml:0
msgid ""
"How can you measure software’s energy consumption? And does it make a "
"difference? We are working to make free software more sustainable."
msgstr ""
"Kako lahko izmerite porabo energije programske opreme? In kakšna je razlika? "
"Delamo na tem, da naredimo prosto programsko opremo bolj trajnostno."

#: i18n/en.yaml:0
msgid "Blauer Engel for Free and Open Source Software"
msgstr "Modri angel za prosto in odprtokodno programsko opremo"

#: i18n/en.yaml:0
msgid ""
"Eco-labels for products are used widely already. But how can they be "
"transferred to software? What criteria is relevant? We need more pioneers to "
"find out how we can make software sustainable."
msgstr ""
"Ekološke oznake za izdelke se že pogosto uporabljajo. Ampak kako lahko "
"nanaša na programsko opremo? Katera merila so pomembna? Potrebujemo več "
"pionirjev, da ugotovimo, kako lahko naredimo programsko opremo trajnostno."

#: i18n/en.yaml:0
msgid "Learn More"
msgstr "Poučite se več"

#: i18n/en.yaml:0
msgid "KDE Eco Handbook"
msgstr "Priročnik KDE Eco"

#: i18n/en.yaml:0
msgid "About This Website"
msgstr "O tem spletišču"

#: i18n/en.yaml:0
msgid ""
"This website is open-source. Source code and asset licenses can be found in "
"the [KDE Eco Repository](https://invent.kde.org/websites/eco-kde-org). This "
"website was checked by the [greenwebfoundation.org](https://www."
"thegreenwebfoundation.org/green-web-check/?url=https%3A%2F%2Feco.kde.org) "
"and is labelled \"Hosted Green\". Website is hosted by: Hetzner Online AG. "
"Supporting evidence for this hoster’s claims: [Sustainability Page](https://"
"www.hetzner.com/unternehmen/umweltschutz)."
msgstr ""
"To spletno mesto je odprtokodno. Izvorno kodo in licence za sredstva najdete "
"v [KDE Eco Repository](https://invent.kde.org/websites/eco-kde-org). To "
"spletno mesto je preveril [greenwebfoundation.org](https://www."
"thegreenwebfoundation.org/green-web-check/?url=https%3A%2F%2Feco.kde.org) in "
"je označeno kot \"Hosted Green\" . Spletno mesto gosti: Hetzner Online AG. "
"Podporni dokazi za trditve tega gostitelja: [Trajnostna stran](https://www."
"hetzner.com/unternehmen/umweltschutz)."

#: i18n/en.yaml:0
msgid "Plots of real time measurements using KDE’s LabPlot."
msgstr "Grafi sprotnih meritev z uporabo KDE's LabPlot."

#: i18n/en.yaml:0
msgid "Okular Awarded Blue Angel Ecolabel"
msgstr "Okular je bil nagrajen z ekološko značko Modri angel"

#: i18n/en.yaml:0
msgid ""
"In 2022, KDE’s popular multi-platform PDF reader and universal document "
"viewer Okular became the first ever eco-certified computer program!"
msgstr ""
"V letu 2022 je bil popularni večplatformni KDE-jev bralnik PDF datotek in "
"univerzalnih dokumentov Okular sploh prvi ekološko potrjeni računalniški "
"program!"

